hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"12","On prayer. Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought them - meaning the prayers - to his people, he left them alone until, when the sun passed the middle of the sky, it was announced among them: Prayer in congregation. So they gathered for that, in alarm, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in four rak'ahs in which he did not recite aloud, with Jibril standing before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing before the people; the people followed their Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed Jibril, peace be upon him. Then he left them alone until, when the sun slanted while white and clear, it was announced among them: Prayer in congregation. They gathered for that, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in four rak'ahs, shorter than the Zuhr prayer; then Ibn al-Muthanna mentioned the same as he had mentioned about Zuhr. He said: Then he turned away from them until, when the sun had set, it was announced among them: Prayer in congregation. They gathered for that, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in three rak'ahs, reciting aloud in two rak'ahs and not reciting aloud in the third; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood before the people, and Jibril stood before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he mentioned the same as he had mentioned about Asr, until, when the twilight came and the night prayer was delayed, it was announced among them: Prayer in congregation. They gathered for that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in four rak'ahs, reciting aloud in two and not reciting aloud in two - mentioning the same as he mentioned about Maghrib. He said: They spent the night not knowing whether anything would be added to that or not, until, when dawn broke, it was announced among them: Prayer in congregation. They gathered for that, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in two rak'ahs in which he recited aloud at length, with Jibril, peace be upon him, standing before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing before the people; the people followed their Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and their Prophet followed Jibril."
"13","Al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Juhani narrated to us; Waki' said: I think it is from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten the daytime prayer on a cloudy day, and delay the Maghrib."
"14","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu Mijlaz, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Umar to forbid urinating facing the qiblah of the mosque."
"15","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Muradi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, that Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him that there were nine mosques in Madinah besides the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whose people would hear the adhan of Bilal in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pray in their mosques: the nearest of them, the mosque of Banu Amr ibn Mabdhul of Banu al-Najjar, the mosque of Banu Sa'idah, the mosque of Banu Ubayd, the mosque of Banu Salamah, the mosque of Banu Rabih of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, the mosque of Banu Zurayq, the mosque of Banu Ghifar, the mosque of Aslam, and the mosque of Juhaynah - with doubt about the ninth."
"16","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from al-Hadrami, from a man of the Ansar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you finds a louse while praying, let him not throw it away, but let him wrap it up until he finishes his prayer. Abu Dawud said: It was narrated from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, Anas ibn Malik and others that they used to kill lice and fleas during prayer."
"17","Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that the delegation of Thaqif came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a dome was pitched for them at the rear of the mosque so they could watch the prayer of the Muslims, their bowing and their prostration. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, would you lodge them in the mosque while they are polytheists? He said: The earth does not become impure; only the son of Adam becomes impure."
"18","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Muradi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab; Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me that Abu Sufyan used to enter the mosque in Madinah while he was a disbeliever - except that such is not permissible for him in the Sacred Mosque, because of what Allah said: The polytheists are impure, so let them not approach the Sacred Mosque - the verse."
